{"id":"lesson-src-92b0fe7e4ac8ee","moduleNumber":776,"headword":"angry","title":"Angry","subtitle":"生氣、憤怒、火大、不滿——哪些詞真的接近 angry？","description":"生氣、憤怒、火大、不滿——哪些詞真的接近 angry？","words":[{"order":1,"word":"Irate","meaning":"憤怒的；非常生氣的","note":"較正式，常形容顧客、乘客、家長或公眾因服務、錯誤或不公平情況而非常生氣。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"An angry customer demanded a full refund.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"irate","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"irate","explanation":"投訴顧客的正式強烈用法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"強度較低。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"太日常。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"意義較廣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"aggressive","explanation":"是行為。"},{"letter":"F","text":"frustrated","explanation":"是受挫。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Several angry passengers complained after the flight was cancelled.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"irate","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"irate","explanation":"passenger complaint 語境自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"也可，但 irate 更常見於投訴語境。"},{"letter":"C","text":"mad","explanation":"太口語。"},{"letter":"D","text":"bitter","explanation":"長期怨恨。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hostile","explanation":"敵對態度。"},{"letter":"F","text":"emotional","explanation":"太廣。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"The manager received calls from angry parents throughout the morning.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"irate","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"irate","explanation":"正式描述憤怒投訴者。"},{"letter":"B","text":"cross","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annoyed","explanation":"較輕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"可能是難過。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resentful","explanation":"偏長期。"},{"letter":"F","text":"impatient","explanation":"核心不同。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Furious","meaning":"極度憤怒的；暴怒的","note":"非常常見的強烈說法，表示比一般 angry 強很多。","example":"這裡是否需要比 angry 明顯更強烈的「非常生氣」？","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"She was extremely angry when she found out that the money was missing.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"furious","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"furious","explanation":"極度憤怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"可能不夠強。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"重點不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"offended","explanation":"重點是被冒犯。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"He was angry with the company for sharing his private information.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"furious","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"furious","explanation":"嚴重事件下強烈憤怒自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"mad","explanation":"也可，但較口語。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"強度不足。"},{"letter":"D","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太弱。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bitter","explanation":"偏長期。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"Residents were angry after the council approved the project without consultation.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"furious","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"furious","explanation":"公眾強烈憤怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"upset","explanation":"太廣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annoyed","explanation":"偏輕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"hostile","explanation":"是敵意態度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"可能有，但不是核心。"},{"letter":"F","text":"emotional","explanation":"太廣。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Enraged","meaning":"被激怒的；暴怒的","note":"表示某件事令一個人進入非常強烈的憤怒狀態。比 angry 強烈，也常暗示「被某事激怒」。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"People were angry when they discovered that the company had hidden the safety problem.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"enraged","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"enraged","explanation":"被事件激起強烈憤怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"太廣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resentful","explanation":"偏持續。"},{"letter":"F","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The decision to cut emergency services made local residents extremely angry.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"enraged","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"enraged","explanation":"明確是決定把人激怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"也很接近。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太弱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"cross","explanation":"太日常。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hostile","explanation":"不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bitter","explanation":"更長期。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"He became angry after seeing how the animals had been treated.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"enraged","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"enraged","explanation":"強烈道德憤怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"不夠強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"upset","explanation":"可能偏傷心。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mad","explanation":"較口語。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Livid","meaning":"氣炸的；怒不可遏的","note":"非正式但很常見的強烈用法，尤其英式英語中常表示「氣到不行」。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"She was absolutely angry when nobody told her the meeting had been moved.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"livid","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"livid","explanation":"「氣炸」的自然強烈用法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"太廣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"offended","explanation":"未必是被冒犯。"},{"letter":"F","text":"frustrated","explanation":"不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"He was angry about being charged twice for the same order.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"livid","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"livid","explanation":"強烈口語憤怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"irate","explanation":"也可，較正式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annoyed","explanation":"偏輕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mad","explanation":"也可，尤其美式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bitter","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"My parents were angry when they saw the damage to the car.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"livid","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"livid","explanation":"強烈而自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"cross","explanation":"強度不足。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annoyed","explanation":"強度不足。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"可用但不一定表示怒氣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hostile","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resentful","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Incensed","meaning":"極為憤怒的；被激怒的","note":"較正式，常表示因不公平、冒犯、政策或行為而強烈憤怒。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Customers were angry by the company's refusal to honour the guarantee.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"incensed","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"incensed","explanation":"因不合理行為而強烈憤怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太弱。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"太口語。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mad","explanation":"較口語。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"frustrated","explanation":"只表示挫折。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Residents were angry at the decision to close the park without warning.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"incensed","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"incensed","explanation":"正式、強烈的公眾憤怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"也可。"},{"letter":"C","text":"upset","explanation":"太廣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"annoyed","explanation":"較弱。"},{"letter":"E","text":"bitter","explanation":"偏長期。"},{"letter":"F","text":"hostile","explanation":"不同。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"Teachers were angry by claims that they had not worked hard enough.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"incensed","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"incensed","explanation":"被不公平／冒犯性說法激怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"offended","explanation":"也可能，但重點更偏受辱。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太弱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"cross","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"emotional","explanation":"太廣。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"Infuriated","meaning":"被激怒的；氣憤至極的","note":"表示某件事使人極度生氣。和 enraged 很接近，但 infuriated 特別常直接指「被某件事激怒」。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"She was angry by the repeated billing errors.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"infuriated","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"infuriated","explanation":"重複錯誤令她極為生氣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"太廣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"有相關但不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The referee's decision made the fans extremely angry.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"infuriated","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"infuriated","explanation":"直接表示某件事把人激怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"強度不足。"},{"letter":"C","text":"upset","explanation":"不夠精準。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mad","explanation":"也可但較口語。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hostile","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bitter","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"He was angry with the bank for freezing his account without explanation.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"infuriated","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"infuriated","explanation":"強烈而直接。"},{"letter":"B","text":"cross","explanation":"太弱。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太弱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"resentful","explanation":"偏持久怨恨。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"emotional","explanation":"太廣。"}]}]},{"order":7,"word":"Seething","meaning":"怒火中燒的；強忍怒氣的","note":"表示內心非常憤怒，但不一定立刻爆發。常帶有「表面壓住，內心怒火翻騰」的感覺。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"She was angry but remained silent throughout the meeting.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"seething","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"seething","explanation":"內心非常憤怒但壓住。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"很生氣，但沒有「強忍」意味。"},{"letter":"C","text":"irate","explanation":"常更外顯。"},{"letter":"D","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"E","text":"cross","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"F","text":"aggressive","explanation":"行為概念。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"He walked out calmly, although he was extremely angry inside.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"seething","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"seething","explanation":"內在怒火最精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"livid","explanation":"強烈但不特別表示壓抑。"},{"letter":"C","text":"mad","explanation":"太一般。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"太廣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"hostile","explanation":"不同。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"She sat at her desk angry about what had happened but said nothing.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"seething","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"seething","explanation":"安靜但怒火中燒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"太弱。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"太輕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"irate","explanation":"常見於外顯投訴。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bitter","explanation":"偏長期。"}]}]},{"order":8,"word":"Mad","meaning":"生氣的；火大的","note":"在美式英語中很常用作 angry 的近義詞，尤其是 mad at someone / mad about something。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Are you angry at me?","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"mad","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"mad","explanation":"美式口語中非常自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"太強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"irate","explanation":"太正式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"cross","explanation":"偏英式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"annoyed","explanation":"較輕。"},{"letter":"F","text":"upset","explanation":"也可但更廣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"He got angry when his brother borrowed the car without asking.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"mad","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"mad","explanation":"美式日常生氣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"enraged","explanation":"過強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"incensed","explanation":"過正式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"seething","explanation":"需要強忍怒火語感。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hostile","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bitter","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"She is still angry about what happened yesterday.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"mad","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"mad","explanation":"美式口語自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"cross","explanation":"英式也可能。"},{"letter":"C","text":"furious","explanation":"可能過強。"},{"letter":"D","text":"irate","explanation":"不合此日常語境。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"aggressive","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":9,"word":"Cross","meaning":"生氣的；不高興的","note":"英式英語常見，通常比 angry 稍輕，尤其適合日常小衝突、責備或不滿。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Dad was angry with me for forgetting to lock the door.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"cross","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cross","explanation":"英式日常、輕度生氣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"過強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"incensed","explanation":"過正式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"livid","explanation":"過強。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resentful","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"hostile","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The teacher looked angry when the class would not stop talking.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"cross","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cross","explanation":"日常輕度不滿。"},{"letter":"B","text":"enraged","explanation":"太強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"irate","explanation":"太正式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"seething","explanation":"需要壓抑強烈怒氣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"upset","explanation":"可能不夠精準。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bitter","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"Don't be angry with me; I didn't know the rule.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"cross","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cross","explanation":"英式口語非常自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"太強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"infuriated","explanation":"太強。"},{"letter":"D","text":"irate","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"不完全等同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"offended","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":10,"word":"Annoyed","meaning":"惱怒的；不耐煩的；有點生氣的","note":"通常比 angry 輕，表示因麻煩、打擾、錯誤或重複問題而生氣或不耐煩。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"I was angry because the train was twenty minutes late again.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"annoyed","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"annoyed","explanation":"延誤引起的輕度惱火。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"通常太強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"enraged","explanation":"太強。"},{"letter":"D","text":"incensed","explanation":"太正式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"upset","explanation":"可用但較廣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bitter","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"She became angry when her phone kept making the same notification sound.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"annoyed","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"annoyed","explanation":"重複煩擾的典型用法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"livid","explanation":"過強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"seething","explanation":"過強。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mad","explanation":"可用但較一般。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hostile","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resentful","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"He sounded angry when I asked him the same question for the third time.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"annoyed","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"annoyed","explanation":"被重複問題煩到。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"太強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"irate","explanation":"太正式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"cross","explanation":"也可能，偏英式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"bitter","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"aggressive","explanation":"是語氣／行為風格。"}]}]},{"order":11,"word":"Upset","meaning":"不高興的；生氣／受困擾的","note":"範圍比 angry 廣，可以表示難過、受傷、擔心或生氣。只有在上下文明確表示不滿或憤怒時，才可接近 angry。","example":"這裡的 upset 是否明確包含「生氣／不滿」，而不是主要表示傷心？","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"She was angry with him for not replying to her messages.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"upset","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"upset","explanation":"在 with someone 結構中可表示不滿／生氣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"可能過強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"irate","explanation":"太正式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"seething","explanation":"太強。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"hostile","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Parents were angry about the sudden change to the school schedule.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"upset","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"upset","explanation":"可表示不滿、受困擾。"},{"letter":"B","text":"livid","explanation":"更強。"},{"letter":"C","text":"incensed","explanation":"更正式且更強。"},{"letter":"D","text":"annoyed","explanation":"也可，但較偏煩擾。"},{"letter":"E","text":"bitter","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"aggressive","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"He was clearly angry after hearing that the decision had been made without him.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"upset","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"upset","explanation":"可涵蓋不高興、生氣和受傷感。"},{"letter":"B","text":"enraged","explanation":"強度可能過高。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cross","explanation":"較輕且偏英式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"irate","explanation":"太正式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impatient","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"emotional","explanation":"太廣。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Frustrated","zh":"受挫不等於生氣 Frustrated 是因無法達成目標或事情不順而挫折；它可以導致 anger，但核心不同。","point":""},{"word":"Offended","zh":"被冒犯不等於生氣 Offended 表示因言行不尊重而感到受辱或不悅，可以同時生氣，但不是同義。","point":""},{"word":"Aggressive","zh":"具攻擊性不等於感到憤怒 Aggressive 描述行為方式；一個人可以 angry 但不 aggressive。","point":""},{"word":"Hostile","zh":"敵意不等於當下生氣 Hostile 表示敵對、不友善，可以是持續態度。","point":""},{"word":"Bitter","zh":"怨恨不等於一般憤怒 Bitter 常是長期的怨憤、失望或不滿。","point":""},{"word":"Resentful","zh":"心懷怨恨不等於單純生氣 Resentful 強調對不公平待遇長期介意。","point":""},{"word":"Impatient","zh":"不耐煩不一定是生氣 Impatient 是不願等待或希望事情更快發生。","point":""},{"word":"Emotional","zh":"情緒激動不等於憤怒 可以是悲傷、興奮、感動等很多不同情緒。","point":""}],"sourceFile":"/synonyms/source/angry_close_synonyms_material.md","priorityRank":776,"omittedExercises":0}